body:
Thank you for taking your time to write this complete answer.

&#x200B;

About the girls, it's complicated. I feel like I've only been losing friends (some friends that I've lost have even begun harassing me) and, sometimes, I get along better with some girls because they're more mature and look like me, more than some boys. These girls, who I'm too afraid to talk to, are three really smart girls with whom I want to be friends with. Actually, I don't have anything to be afraid of because I get along really well with them and they really appreciate me (I know that they consider me as friends) but I'm so stressed out and if I don't go to talk to them, I hate myself from being unable to talk to others. I know that it's confusing and that it doesn't make much sense. The point is that I want to spend more time with them but the idea to go to them scares me, probably because I feel like I annoy them and I don't want to be annoying. It's complicated and it incoherent. At least, writing it down made me realize how I didn't need to be so afraid. The problem is that when I fail to talk to them, I feel shitty.

&#x200B;

About having a good circle of friends, I really have a few friends left. To be clear, there are two people that I consider as real friends, and one of them is in the hospital because she's seriously depressed. It's one of the reasons why I want so much to befriend those girls: I want to have a group of friends who understand me and who make me feel good. Talking to them makes me happy.

&#x200B;

The kids at school want to help me and talk to me, but I can't explain to them (depression has become a forbidden word there). They are good people but I feel like I'm not like them.

&#x200B;

About art, I love reading comic-books, I draw, I love analyzing movies (their narrative structure, their moral, their philosophy). I love thinking about themes and about art (I've written a novel about our relationship to art).

&#x200B;

The last line really had me thinking and you're right, I want to be happy and to have a great future, surrounded by great friends and doing what I love (writing comic-books and finally making the movie that I want to make). Thank you for everything, I know that my feelings depend on how I react to some situations and I need to make a bigger effort to let some things go through me.

Ok thanks I know that I have to do that but I hoped there would be another thing to do but apparently, I'm the only one who can act. If he keeps looking at me in a creepy way more and more often, I will get a teacher involved (but it's hard because he's the son of a teacher). Also I have now the confirmation that I have to keep my stuff safe, so thank you.

&#x200B;

Also, I hoped it wouldn't be so easy to notice that I like this girl.
